.SS "int wget_dns_init (wget_dns ** dns)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdns\fP Pointer to return newly allocated and initialized wget_dns instance 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
WGET_E_SUCCESS if OK, WGET_E_MEMORY if out-of-memory or WGET_E_INVALID if the mutex initialization failed\&.
.RE
.PP
Allocates and initializes a wget_dns instance\&. \fRdns\fP may be NULL for the purpose of initializing the global structures\&. 
.SS "void wget_dns_free (wget_dns ** dns)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI[in/out]\fP dns Pointer to wget_dns instance that will be freed and NULLified\&.
.RE
.PP
Free the resources allocated by \fBwget_dns_init()\fP\&. \fRdns\fP may be NULL for the purpose of freeing the global structures\&. 
.SS "void wget_dns_set_timeout (wget_dns * dns, int timeout)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdns\fP The wget_dns instance to set the timeout 
.br
\fItimeout\fP The timeout value\&.
.RE
.PP
Set the timeout (in milliseconds) for the DNS queries\&.

.PP
This is the maximum time to wait until we get a response from the server\&.

.PP
Warning: For standard getaddrinfo() a timeout can't be set in a portable way\&. So this functions currently is a no-op\&.

.PP
The following two values are special:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR0\fP: No timeout, immediate\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR-1\fP: Infinite timeout\&. Wait indefinitely\&. 
.PP

.SS "void wget_dns_set_cache (wget_dns * dns, wget_dns_cache * cache)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdns\fP A \fRwget_dns\fP instance, created by \fBwget_dns_init()\fP\&. 
.br
\fIcache\fP A \fRwget_dns_cache\fP instance
.RE
.PP
Enable or disable DNS caching for the DNS instance provided\&.

.PP
The DNS cache is kept internally in memory, and is used in \fBwget_dns_resolve()\fP to speed up DNS queries\&. 
.SS "wget_dns_cache * wget_dns_get_cache (wget_dns * dns)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdns\fP A \fRwget_dns\fP instance, created by \fBwget_dns_init()\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
1 if DNS caching is enabled, 0 otherwise\&.
.RE
.PP
Tells whether DNS caching is enabled or not\&.

.PP
You can enable and disable DNS caching with wget_dns_set_caching()\&. 
.SS "int wget_dns_cache_ip (wget_dns * dns, const char * ip, const char * name, uint16_t port)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIip\fP IP address of name 
.br
\fIname\fP Domain name, part of the cache's lookup key 
.br
\fIport\fP Port number, part of the cache's lookup key 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
0 on success, < 0 on error
.RE
.PP
Assign an IP address to the name+port key in the DNS cache\&. The \fRname\fP should be lowercase\&. 
.SS "struct addrinfo * wget_dns_resolve (wget_dns * dns, const char * host, uint16_t port, int family, int preferred_family)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdns\fP A \fRwget_dns\fP instance, created by \fBwget_dns_init()\fP\&. 
.br
\fIhost\fP Hostname 
.br
\fIport\fP TCP destination port 
.br
\fIfamily\fP Protocol family AF_INET or AF_INET6 
.br
\fIpreferred_family\fP Preferred protocol family AF_INET or AF_INET6 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A \fRstruct addrinfo\fP structure (defined in libc's \fR<netdb\&.h>\fP)\&. Must be freed by the caller with \fR\fBwget_dns_freeaddrinfo()\fP\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Resolve a host name into its IPv4/IPv6 address\&.

.PP
\fBfamily\fP: Desired address family for the returned addresses\&. This will typically be \fRAF_INET\fP or \fRAF_INET6\fP, but it can be any of the values defined in \fR<socket\&.h>\fP\&. Additionally, \fRAF_UNSPEC\fP means you don't care: it will return any address family that can be used with the specified \fRhost\fP and \fRport\fP\&. If \fBfamily\fP is different than \fRAF_UNSPEC\fP and the specified family is not found, \fIthat's an error condition\fP and thus \fBwget_dns_resolve()\fP will return NULL\&.

.PP
\fBpreferred_family\fP: Tries to resolve addresses of this family if possible\&. This is only honored if \fBfamily\fP (see point above) is \fRAF_UNSPEC\fP\&.

.PP
The returned \fRaddrinfo\fP structure must be freed with \fR\fBwget_dns_freeaddrinfo()\fP\fP\&. 
.SS "void wget_dns_freeaddrinfo (wget_dns * dns, struct addrinfo ** addrinfo)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdns\fP A \fRwget_dns\fP instance, created by \fBwget_dns_init()\fP\&. 
.br
\fI[in/out]\fP addrinfo Value returned by \fRc\fP
.RE
.PP
Release addrinfo, previously returned by \fR\fBwget_dns_resolve()\fP\fP\&. If the underlying \fRdns\fP uses caching, just the reference/pointer is set to NULL\&. 
.SS "void wget_dns_set_stats_callback (wget_dns * dns, wget_dns_stats_callback * fn, void * ctx)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdns\fP A \fRwget_dns\fP instance, created by \fBwget_dns_init()\fP\&. 
.br
\fIfn\fP A \fRwget_dns_stats_callback\fP callback function to receive resolve statistics data 
.br
\fIctx\fP Context data given to \fRfn\fP 
.RE
.PP
Set callback function to be called once DNS statistics for a host are collected 
